========================================================================
A. Potential's contribution to both field equations at f = c^2 g (sympy, exact)
========================================================================
isotropic (all four components equal): True True
2 dU/dg_ii at (1, c^2) = beta0 + 3*beta1*c + 3*beta2*c**2 + beta3*c**3
2 dU/df_ii at (1, c^2) = beta1/c + 3*beta2 + 3*beta3*c + beta4*c**2
matches beta0+3c beta1+3c^2 beta2+c^3 beta3 : True
matches (c b1+3c^2 b2+3c^3 b3+c^4 b4)/c^2   : True

At the aligned point c = 1:
  g-eq flatness form  L_g = beta0 + 3*beta1 + 3*beta2 + beta3
  f-eq flatness form  L_f = beta1 + 3*beta2 + 3*beta3 + beta4
  U(1,1) = V(1)           = beta0 + 4*beta1 + 6*beta2 + 4*beta3 + beta4
  L_g == V(1) - T(#8) : True   (#8 sec.2: 'V(1) = T' is the g-eq)
  L_f == T(#8)        : True
  V(1) == L_g + L_f   : True   (Pascal: C(4,n) = C(3,n) + C(3,n-1))

Even/odd tadpoles under the exchange g <-> f (massless = even, X = odd, #8 sec.3):
  even (sources the massless graviton's Lambda): beta0 + 4*beta1 + 6*beta2 + 4*beta3 + beta4
  odd  (relative mode):                           beta0 + 2*beta1 - 2*beta3 - beta4
  palindrome beta_n = beta_{4-n}:  odd -> 0    even -> 2*beta0 + 8*beta1 + 6*beta2
  palindrome: L_g -> beta0 + 4*beta1 + 3*beta2   L_f -> beta0 + 4*beta1 + 3*beta2   V(1) -> 2*beta0 + 8*beta1 + 6*beta2

========================================================================
B. Counting conditions on (beta0..beta4) (exact linear algebra)
========================================================================
generic bimetric, flat aligned vacuum: rank 2 -> free betas 3
palindrome alone:                       rank 2 -> free betas 3
palindrome + flat aligned vacuum:       rank 3 -> free betas 2
  conditions added by flatness beyond the palindrome: 1
flatness forms restricted to the palindromic subspace: [1, 4, 3, 1, 4, 3]  rank 1
is V(1) zero on the generic flat-aligned locus (no palindrome)? True

========================================================================
C. A palindromic theory whose aligned vacuum is not flat: the PM point (#11 sec.7.4)
========================================================================
Lambda_g(c) - Lambda_f(c) at the PM point: 0  (zero for every c = 'undetermined ratio', the published PM hallmark)
Lambda(c) [units m^4] = 3*beta_2*(alpha**2*c**2 + 1)/(M_g**2*alpha**2)
alpha = 1 betas: [3*beta_2, 0, beta_2, 0, 3*beta_2] palindromic: True
  aligned (c=1) Lambda = 6*beta_2/M_g**2   T_pal = beta0+4beta1+3beta2 = 6*beta_2
  real zeros of Lambda(c) at alpha=1: []

